WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.735
You've discussed power and labor

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.518
shortages, but now everyone is more

00:00:03.518 --> 00:00:05.517
focused on nuclear energy. Your stance

00:00:05.517 --> 00:00:07.349
has always been very clear: safety,

00:00:07.349 --> 00:00:09.130
nuclear waste disposal, and social

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.107
consensus. Once these three principles

00:00:11.107 --> 00:00:12.917
are confirmed, can it move forward?

00:00:12.917 --> 00:00:14.141
However,

00:00:14.141 --> 00:00:15.949
>> I know you hold an open attitude, but

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.852
there are two types of openness: active

00:00:17.852 --> 00:00:19.792
openness and passive openness. One is:

00:00:19.792 --> 00:00:21.854
"I'm facing a power shortage, so I must

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:24.043
strongly push for nuclear power." The

00:00:24.043 --> 00:00:25.063
other is: "

00:00:25.063 --> 00:00:26.841
>> I'm not that supportive, but if you

00:00:26.841 --> 00:00:28.816
have a request, I'll cooperate; I won't

00:00:28.816 --> 00:00:31.294
block it. If there's a need, I'll do it

00:00:31.294 --> 00:00:33.333
." Regarding your current stance on

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.467
nuclear power, is it an active attitude

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.218
—active openness—or passive

00:00:37.218 --> 00:00:37.811
openness?

00:00:37.811 --> 00:00:40.143
>> Whether I am active or passive, it is

00:00:40.143 --> 00:00:42.291
perhaps best left to the public to

00:00:42.291 --> 00:00:43.435
judge accurately.

00:00:43.435 --> 00:00:46.560
>> But my attitude is very clear. We

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.297
should not use ideology to exclude any

00:00:49.297 --> 00:00:50.591
source of energy.

00:00:50.591 --> 00:00:51.715
>> Hmm.

00:00:51.715 --> 00:00:53.584
>> And we should not, for the sake of

00:00:53.584 --> 00:00:54.752
short-term benefits,

00:00:54.752 --> 00:00:56.926
>> disregard the sustainability of our

00:00:56.926 --> 00:00:59.124
environment. Therefore, as long as it

00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:01.268
meets safety standards, has a solution

00:01:01.268 --> 00:01:03.411
for waste, and holds social consensus,

00:01:03.411 --> 00:01:05.769
we will move forward with it. Secondly,

00:01:05.769 --> 00:01:08.300
as everyone should be able to see, the

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.896
process for restarting nuclear power is

00:01:10.896 --> 00:01:13.362
underway because the Legislative Yuan

00:01:13.362 --> 00:01:15.634
has passed the law, and the Taiwan

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.970
Power Company has already begun the

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:19.304
restart procedures.

00:01:19.304 --> 00:01:21.282
>> We are a democratic country and a

00:01:21.282 --> 00:01:23.478
society governed by the rule of law.

00:01:23.478 --> 00:01:25.282
>> We must respect public opinion, so we

00:01:25.282 --> 00:01:27.182
will let the process run its course and

00:01:27.182 --> 00:01:28.702
leave the final decision to the

00:01:28.702 --> 00:01:30.598
professionals. Whether

00:01:30.598 --> 00:01:32.450
>> nuclear safety meets the standards,

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.302
whether nuclear waste can indeed be

00:01:34.302 --> 00:01:36.308
solved with no remaining concerns, and

00:01:36.308 --> 00:01:38.315
whether there is social consensus—if

00:01:38.315 --> 00:01:40.373
there is consensus, we will restart; if

00:01:40.373 --> 00:01:42.419
not, we must of course wait.

00:01:42.419 --> 00:01:46.419
>> Wait for advanced nuclear technology.
